       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks like an error. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin. The usual maximum single dose is about 850 mg to 1,000 mg. A dose this high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day in divided doses**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another regimen**, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg per dose.\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, please confirm that. Add the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
